# behavior: a dependency's function whose defaults name a private const, call a private function or name a private enum's variant takes their values when a consumer omits the arguments, directly and through a partial over the function; and a consumer that imports neither a dependency's public model nor its public class omits the arguments whose defaults construct them, directly and through a partial, and calls a partial whose preset constructs the model, each call taking the constructed value, including the private field the model's declaration defaults and a field argument naming a private const
# expect-stdout:
#   flat of size 2cm
#   flat of size 3cm
#   gloss
#   note of size 4
#   3
#   6
#   t: ace of size 4

from pub::shapes import build, count, default_build, finish, show, stacked_twice, tag_ace


def main() -> None:
    println(build(2))
    println(default_build())
    println(finish())
    println(show())
    println(count())
    println(stacked_twice())
    println(tag_ace(tag="t:"))
